weave-knee trial v1
fanout: 10
seed: 2
weaver: claude-sonnet-5
judge: claude-sonnet-5
quality: 3
narrative:
  Mirgri turns on a single loop that closes back on itself, ten modules passing the same pressure around a ring until it returns to where it started.

  At the head sits Nexvar, the vault. Nexvar refuses new writes while its own sweep is running, evicts anything left unclaimed after 11 ticks, and acts only once 3 of its peers countersign. What Nexvar cannot absorb it delegates as overflow to Saxvar.

  Saxvar, the index, evicts anything left unclaimed after 7 ticks, keeps only digests of what it carries and never the bodies, and, like Nexvar, refuses new writes while its own sweep is running. What Saxvar evicts, it streams onward to Varbra.

  Varbra, the sampler, refuses new writes while its sweep is running and keeps digests rather than bodies; when a handoff fails, Varbra retries it at most 4 times before parking it. Varbra's part in the loop is to signal backpressure to Osthul.

  Osthul, the scheduler, acts only once 4 of its peers countersign, answers reads from its newest snapshot only, and refuses new writes while its own sweep is running. Osthul reports missed heartbeats to Felost.

  Felost, the registry, evicts anything left unclaimed after 7 ticks, retries a failed handoff at most 4 times before parking it, and refuses new writes while its sweep is running. Felost publishes its sweep verdicts to Varost.

  Varost, the monitor, refuses new writes while its own sweep is running, keeps digests of what it carries and never the bodies, and evicts anything left unclaimed after 9 ticks. Varost hands its sealed ledger to Zindor.

  Zindor, the broker, retries a failed handoff at most 4 times before parking it, answers reads from its newest snapshot only, and acts only once 3 of its peers countersign. Zindor delegates overflow to Pambra.

  Pambra, the ledger, retries a failed handoff at most 4 times before parking it, refuses new writes while its own sweep is running, and answers reads from its newest snapshot only. Pambra streams its evictions to Kelfel.

  Kelfel, the cache, acts only once 5 of its peers countersign, evicts anything left unclaimed after 7 ticks, and retries a failed handoff at most 3 times before parking it. Kelfel signals backpressure to Tolsax.

  Tolsax, the throttle, retries a failed handoff at most 1 time before parking it, keeps digests of what it carries and never the bodies, and evicts anything left unclaimed after 12 ticks. Tolsax closes the ring by reporting missed heartbeats back to Nexvar, the vault where the loop began.

  Across the ten, the same handful of behaviors recur in different combinations: a sweep that locks out writes, a countersign threshold that gates action, an eviction clock, a digest-only memory, a bounded retry before parking, and a snapshot-only read. What differs module to module is which of these each one carries, and where in the ring its outgoing relation sends the consequence next — overflow passed twice, from Nexvar to Saxvar and from Zindor to Pambra; evictions streamed twice, from Saxvar to Varbra and from Pambra to Kelfel; backpressure signaled twice, from Varbra to Osthul and from Kelfel to Tolsax; heartbeats reported twice, from Osthul to Felost and from Tolsax to Nexvar; and a single verdict and a single ledger passed once each, from Felost to Varost and from Varost to Zindor, at the ring's midpoint.
